        "explanation": "To satisfy formal differential privacy guarantees, the Topics API introduces 5% random noise: with a 5% probability, the browser picks a topic uniformly at random from the entire 469-topic taxonomy instead of returning the user's true calculated top topic. This mathematical noise ensures plausible deniability."
